    "description": "TO VIEW THIS HOME:\nPlease email us through this post\nKEY DETAILS:\n\u2022Bedrooms: 5 Bedrooms\n\u2022Bathrooms: 3 Bathrooms\n\u2022Property Type: Single-Family Home\n\u2022Lease Duration: Long-term or short-term - 1 Year Preferred\n\u2022Pets Policy: Pets Welcome\n\u2022Laundry: Washer and Dryer in unit\n\u2022Detached 365 sq. ft. backyard studio/flex space \u2014 ideal for a home office, art studio, gym, workshop, or additional storage\nDESCRIPTION:\nREMODELED HOUSE WITH YARD AND 2-CAR PARKING! PLUS, A DETACHED 365 SQ. FT. BACKYARD STUDIO / FLEX SPACE!\nA rare bonus: a separate stand-alone building in the private backyard, providing approximately 365 sq. ft. of additional flexible space. Ideal for a home office, art studio, creative workspace, gym, workshop, or substantial storage.\n\u2022Yes, you get both the home and the detached studio!\n\u2022Living room and dining area with desirable, open floor plan\n\u2022Hardwood (laminated) flooring throughout the home\n\u2022Remodeled gas kitchen with granite countertops and all stainless appliances\n\u2022Three remodeled, tiled baths; one bath in the master suite\n\u2022Five bedrooms, with generous closet spaces\n\u2022In-unit washer and dryer\n\u2022Newer interior paint\n\u2022Newer exterior paint\n\u2022Refinished windows and blinds\n\u2022Cozy and sunny private fenced-in yard for you and your pet\n\u2022Two-car, side-by-side off-street parking\nLOCATION:\nThis renovated, single-family home with 2-car parking is situated in one of the city's most charming and diverse neighborhoods. Mission Street provides a cornucopia of great coffeehouses, bars, restaurants, grocery stores, and shops, all within a few blocks from your new home. Short distance to SFSU and CCSF. A commuter's dream; the financial district is approximately fifteen minutes away. It is a three-minute drive to 280 or 101 freeways for a quick commute to the valley. The BART station is at Balboa Park Station, and public transportation is 